  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">COUNCIL OF EUROPE ACTION PLAN FOR GEORGIA 2020-2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Council of Europe&#x2019;s Action Plan for Georgia 2020-2023 aims to bring Georgia&#x2019;s legislation, institutions and practice into line with European standards in the areas of human rights, the rule of law and democracy. This includes reforms to enhance the implementation of the European Convention on Human Rights (ECHR) and the European Court of Human Rights (ECtHR) case-law at national level, align national legislation and practice of anti-discrimination with European standards, promote gender equality, enhance the independence of the judicial system, improve electoral legislation, enhance the protection of economic and social rights, facilitate civil society participation in decision making at all levels, and increase dialogue and confidence building between divided communities.</narrative>
  </description>
